      "math_academy_id": "e-5394",
      "problem": "What is the polar equation of the curve shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/0ad44bfa452da482fff5f579f1be9569670f7ad8da347314bcb63f618eaf3d2a.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The diagram shows a circle of radius $|a| = |-4.5|=4.5$ centered at the point $(0,-4.5).$ \n\nIn polar coordinates, the equation of such a circle is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-4.5)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
